WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.901
-You have not always been
a writer

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:03.836
and an actor and a comedian.

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:06.339
You did some work at the mall
over the years.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:09.442
-I did. I went to the mall
the other day, locally,

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:12.245
where I live,
and it was a really dead mall.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:14.180
There were only
like three things in it now,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.284
and just a lot of posters that
were sort of positive messages.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.920
They had shuttered-up stores.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.990
And they were like giant
greeting cards,

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:29.195
but I spent so much of
my high school years in the mall

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:33.800
in Orlando area,
and I worked at York Steakhouse.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.669
And York Steakhouse, you know,
I loved restaurant work

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.472
because I hated being bored
and I loved anything

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:41.440
that was just like a hustle
and I was just sweating,

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.443
and I guess that's why I loved
"SNL" so much.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:46.179
But I just loved,
like, having a lot to do.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:50.950
And I had this manager
that just, you know,

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.919
he always supported
my performing career

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.588
and everything,
and he came to me.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.990
He was always trying to, like,
throw me a bone on anything that

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.294
was performative of any kind,
and so he -- I was, you know,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:05.431
serving the food and being
the cashier, and he came one day

00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:08.033
and he was like,
"We're doing a promotion

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:11.070
with Strawberry Shortcake,
the character.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.773
And what if you played
Strawberry Shortcake

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:19.879
in a costume outside
the restaurant, inside the mall

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:23.382
and give helium balloons to
the kids and try to get people

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.718
in for the special
that we are having?"

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.387
And so I did it
for like three weeks,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.322
and it was really exciting. Yes,
I was exactly in that costume.

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.491
-Here's Strawberry Shortcake
for those who don't remember.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:35.195
-I had like four freckles
on each cheek,

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.229
and I had a little --
a bunch of blush,

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.966
and I had this giant red wig,
and it was very clown-like

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:43.269
but like a fem clown.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:47.907
And I -- Every week --
this is how old I am --

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:50.577
there used to be a Wurlitzer
organ store in the mall.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.212
And so every week, on Sundays,
they would take,

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.915
in the freight elevator,
they would send the organ up --

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.483
that's what she said...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.487
...and they'd send the organ up
the freight elevator.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:05.491
And then they would have these
old men -- old men and old women

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:08.994
there and they'd have desserts
free and coffee, and then

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:12.264
the guy would play the organ
for a couple hours at night,

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.800
and then they would all die.
No, I'm just kidding.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:15.869
[ Laughter ]
They wouldn't die.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:19.739
And so I --
One night he comes out,

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:21.540
and I'm still
Strawberry Shortcake.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.975
And he goes, "Come here."

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:26.112
He goes, "I just -- I just love
the way you sing.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:28.581
What if you sang something
for all these people?"

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.150
And I said, "Well, I didn't
rehearse any of this."

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.352
I don't even know if he's got
anything that I know.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.889
And I was real nervous,
and he pulled me in there,

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:40.126
and he had the piano book, and
the only song of about 500 songs

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:43.730
I knew in the piano book,
in the organ book, which I sang,

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.199
including like four verses of,
was this.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.734
Picture my Strawberry Shortcake.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:55.141
♪ Were you there
when they crucified my Lord? ♪

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.842
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.842 --> 00:03:00.780
♪ Were you there
when they crucified ♪

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.150
And it was just a pan across,
as if it was an "SNL" sketch,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.453
of just a lot of people
being very sad about

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:13.692
this maudlin song with a scary,
little, young, chubby clown

00:03:13.692 --> 00:03:15.695
in front of them singing it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:18.130
It's the stuff of nightmares.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.965
And then I worked in a gift shop
in the mall,

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:23.502
and I used to order Chick-fil-A
chicken and biscuits

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:24.603
in the morning.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.338
I'd volunteer
to go get breakfast.

00:03:26.338 --> 00:03:28.741
I'd run down there,
I'd get chicken and biscuits.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:32.678
I'd get one extra for me,
and then I would eat it

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:35.147
under the escalator
behind the plants,

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:38.050
and then I would come up with,
like, biscuit spackle

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:41.287
across my teeth and pretend
I was really hungry

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:44.023
like, "Let's have breakfast!"

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:48.194
[ Laughter ]
I had a lot of fun in the mall.

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:51.530
-I do like talking to you
about your animals.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.033
You are an animal lover,
a renowned animal lover.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.401
How many pets do you have now?

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.236
-I have two horses.

00:03:57.236 --> 00:04:00.639
I just acquired an old horse
that I used to have,

00:04:00.639 --> 00:04:03.242
and I got a rescue horse
to be her companion.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:07.046
I have four dogs,
and I have a 21-year-old cat.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.481
-Which dog is this?

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.982
-That's Ernie.
-Okay.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:14.386
-And that picture is enjoyable
because it looks like I drooled

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:17.456
all the way down my shirt.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.359
Or he peed on me,
which he did not do.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.295
But Ernie has --
Ernie has an overbite.

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:26.699
He has four -- He's my new dog
I got from California

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:29.168
before I moved to New York
again.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.937
He has a four-teeth overbite.

00:04:31.937 --> 00:04:35.140
It's a real journey.

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.542
-We've got a nice reveal.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.045
So, here's the first one,
and everybody can picture

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:41.981
what a four-toothed overbite
looks like.

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.315
And there you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:46.652
-Yep. That's Ernie.

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.954
And he's got a really weird
personality,

00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.423
and we finally figured him out.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:54.159
At first we thought he was just
a little bit of a Chihuahua

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:57.096
being a jerk and -- because he
started getting real aggressive

00:04:57.096 --> 00:05:00.433
with the other dogs, and then we
realized he's just like a human

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:04.637
that's super awkward and doesn't
have a lot of skills or game,

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.538
so he'll just be like...
[ Barks ]

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:07.806
...when he wants to play,

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:09.208
and so you're always
scolding him,

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.776
thinking he's attacking things,

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:12.644
and then he really
just wants to play,

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:16.715
so I'm really trying to
get to know him

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:18.751
and understand
that he's a weirdo.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.452
-Not a great first-impression
dog.

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:22.655
It seems like you want to spend
some time with him.

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:26.425
-Yeah.
Yeah, we don't want to have --

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:29.194
We have a lot of animals, so if
one starts fighting the other,

00:05:29.194 --> 00:05:34.033
it's pretty much --
it's like a Greek arena.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:36.201
You just watch
everyone kill each other.

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:38.571
-Congratulations on everything.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:42.074
Best of luck this weekend
on your Emmy nomination,

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:44.343
and it's always just such
a delight to see you, Paula.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:46.578
-Thank you. I love you,
and I wish I could be there.

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:47.913
I'll be there next time.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:49.181
-Alright, we love you too.

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.084
"A.P. Bio" is streaming now
on Peacock.

